<!doctype html>
<!--
  Privacy.

  **A mandatory App Store listing field, and the reason this page exists at
  all.** The app's design is most of the policy: no account, no sync, and a
  garden kept in the app's own storage. What it does send is said in full —
  what two phones hand each other at a meeting, what a seed's link carries,
  what the web garden keeps of a plant two people agree to share and for how
  long, what the app asks it on starting, and what the site keeps of a
  visitor. Until 24 September this comment said there was no server and no
  network request of the app's own, and the page said the same; the web
  garden made both untrue, and the page was rewritten to Marcus's wording.

  Eight paragraphs, in the order a reader meets the things they describe: the
  phone, the meeting, the storage, the link, the web garden, the asking,
  releasing a plant, and the website last. The keys are numbered in the order
  they were made, so the page reads 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 5. `strings.js` names,
  beside each key, the code its sentence is true of. The eighth was added on
  1 October 2026, the day release began to send a plant to the Wild Fields,
  and is English in every language until it is commissioned.

  Written in the reader's own language like everything else here. Marcus's call,
  6 September 2026: the reader of this page was handed a link by somebody they
  met and is wondering whether it is a scam, so it is the one page where falling
  back to English costs the most.

  No analytics, no font CDN, no third-party anything — which this page then
  says, and would be a poor place to be lying.
-->
